 "title": "empezar, o → ue stem change, dormir, encontrar, mostrar",
 "cards": [
  {
   "title": "empezar = to start",
   "body": "Comenzar ('commence') exists, but empezar is more common. Process: go back to the 'to' form (empezar, -ar), make the form (empeza), then let the stressed e split (empieza).",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I start",
     "es": "empiezo"
    },
    {
     "en": "he / she starts",
     "es": "empieza"
    },
    {
     "en": "When are you starting?",
     "es": "¿Cuándo empiezas?"
    }
   ],
   "t": 0
  },
  {
   "title": "Stressed o splits into ue",
   "body": "The present tense stresses the second-to-last syllable, which makes a root e or o vulnerable: e → ie, o → ue. Poder (to be able) → puedo. El poder = the power (el = the, for masculine words).",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I can",
     "es": "puedo"
    },
    {
     "en": "the power",
     "es": "el poder"
    }
   ],
   "t": 83.9
  },
  {
   "title": "o → ue between languages",
   "body": "Spot it in related words. Rico = rich, nice or tasty.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "port",
     "es": "puerto"
    },
    {
     "en": "force",
     "es": "fuerza"
    },
    {
     "en": "school",
     "es": "escuela"
    },
    {
     "en": "body (corp-)",
     "es": "cuerpo"
    },
    {
     "en": "new (nov-)",
     "es": "nuevo"
    },
    {
     "en": "village / a people",
     "es": "pueblo"
    }
   ],
   "t": 165.8
  },
  {
   "title": "muerte / muerto",
   "body": "Mortgage = 'death pact' (mort = death). A noun is what you can put 'the' in front of: la muerte (death). The describing word is muerto / muerta (dead).",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "death",
     "es": "la muerte"
    },
    {
     "en": "dead",
     "es": "muerto / muerta"
    }
   ],
   "t": 247.2
  },
  {
   "title": "dormir = to sleep",
   "body": "Think dormant, dormitory. Me duermo ('I sleep myself') = I fall asleep.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I sleep",
     "es": "duermo"
    },
    {
     "en": "I'm falling asleep.",
     "es": "Me duermo."
    },
    {
     "en": "he sleeps / they sleep",
     "es": "duerme / duermen"
    }
   ],
   "t": 303.7
  },
  {
   "title": "encontrar = to find (encounter)",
   "body": "A verb form can also be a noun: un encuentro = an encounter; encuentro = I find.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I find it.",
     "es": "Lo encuentro."
    },
    {
     "en": "an encounter",
     "es": "un encuentro"
    }
   ],
   "t": 351.1
  },
  {
   "title": "mostrar → muestro",
   "body": "Una muestra = a sample, sharing a form with muestra (he/she shows). One r, so no roll.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I show",
     "es": "muestro"
    },
    {
     "en": "he shows / they show",
     "es": "muestra / muestran"
    }
   ],
   "t": 416.9
  }
